  "question": {
    "text": "<p>At what <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math>, given half cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8739;</mo><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></math> will have electrode potential of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>282</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;? (Nearest Integer)</p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  },
